   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 154 of the laws of 1921, relating to the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, in relation to paid time off for Port Authority police officers who become ill or injured in the performance of their duties",
    "basePrintNo": "S6274",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6274-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 23, Chap 154 of 1921",
    "lawSection": "Port Authority of New York and New Jersey",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6274          REVISED MEMO 01/18/2018\n\nSPONSOR: LANZA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 154 of the laws of 1921,\nrelating to the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, in relation\nto paid time off for Port Authority police officers who become ill or\ninjured in the performance of their duties\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide paid time off for Port Authority of New York and New Jersey\npolice officers who become ill or injured in the performance of their\nduties.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one: adds a new article 23 to chapter 154 of the laws of 1921 to\nallow members of the police department of the port authority of New York\nand New Jersey to receive full salary if they are injured or fall ill as\na result of fulfilling the duties of their job.  Additionally, the port\nauthority would be liable for all medical expenses incurred by such an\ninjury or illness. Members who are eligible for an accidental disability\nretirement allowance or a performance of duty disability allowance would\nnot be eligible for this provision. Members who are capable of light\npolice duty may be offered a suitable position with the port authority\npolice.\n\nSection two: effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill establishes protection in regards to financial security for\ninjured or ill members of the police department of the port authority\nwho may not otherwise have such protection.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017:S.6274- Referred to Corporations/A.6991 -Passed Assembly\n2016:5.7723- Referred to Corporations/A.9438- Passed Assembly\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect when the state of New Jersey enacts legis-\nlation with identical effect. Should New Jersey have already enacted\nsuch legislation, this act shall take effect immediately.\n",
